<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tonga</h1><p class="st-meta">1845 CE – present · capital Nukuʻalofa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The only Pacific island state never formally colonised, a constitutional monarchy founded by George Tupou I that still rules today.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tonga had long been ruled through the sacred <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tu-i-tonga-empire">Tuʻi Tonga Empire</a> and related chiefly lines, but civil wars broke out in the early 19th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-tupou-i">Tāufaʻāhau</a>, a chief from Haʻapai converted by Wesleyan missionaries, united the islands by 1845 and took the name George Tupou I, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nukualofa">Nukuʻalofa</a> as his capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-tupou-i">George Tupou I</a> issued codes freeing commoners from chiefly obligations in 1862 and granted a constitution in 1875, assisted by the missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirley-baker">Shirley Baker</a>, which remains in force in amended form; later land laws guaranteed every adult male a plot. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tu-i-tonga-empire">Tuʻi Tonga</a> line was ended in 1865. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methodism">Methodism</a> became the dominant faith. From 1900 to 1970 Tonga was a British protected state, governing itself internally, and Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salote-tupou-iii">Sālote Tupou III</a> became widely admired.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Tonga regained full independence in 1970 and joined the Commonwealth. Riots in 2006 hastened reforms, and since 2010 most of parliament has been elected by the people. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupou-vi">Tupou VI</a> has reigned since 2012.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-tonga.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Tonga" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Uelingatoni Ngu Tupoumalohi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tonga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years<